<body>
<div class="page">
  <h1>Singapore PSI predictor</h1>
  <p class="subtitle">Predicted PSI in each region of Singapore and at outdoor recreation areas, based on live readings from NEA. The time frame being shown is always labelled above the map. Click anywhere on the map to check a specific spot.</p>

  <p id="status" class="status">Loading live data...</p>
  <div id="when-chip" class="haze-chip" style="display:none; cursor: default"></div>
  <div id="haze-chip" class="haze-chip" style="display:none" title="Open the regional haze view"></div>
  <div id="map"></div>
  <p id="map-note" class="hint"></p>

  <div class="controls">
    <div class="group" id="fmode-group" style="display:none">
      <span class="group-title">Forecast</span>
      <label><input type="radio" name="fmode" value="hourly" checked>Hour by hour</label>
      <label><input type="radio" name="fmode" value="daily">Tomorrow's average</label>
    </div>
    <div class="group">
      <span class="group-title">View</span>
      <label><input type="radio" name="viewmode" value="sg" checked>Singapore</label>
      <label><input type="radio" name="viewmode" value="regional">Regional haze</label>
    </div>
    <div class="group">
      <span class="group-title">Map style</span>
      <label><input type="radio" name="mapstyle" value="clean" checked>Clean map</label>
      <label><input type="radio" name="mapstyle" value="street">Street map</label>
      <label><input type="checkbox" id="toggle-shade" checked>PSI shading (street map)</label>
    </div>
    <div class="group">
      <span class="group-title">Show</span>
      <label><input type="checkbox" id="toggle-rec" checked><span class="dot rec"></span>Recreation areas</label>
      <label><input type="checkbox" id="toggle-bball"><span class="dot bball"></span>Basketball courts</label>
      <label><input type="checkbox" id="toggle-play"><span class="dot play"></span>Playgrounds</label>
      <label><input type="checkbox" id="toggle-foot"><span class="dot foot"></span>Football fields</label>
      <label><input type="checkbox" id="toggle-comp"><span class="dot comp"></span>Sports complexes</label>
    </div>
    <div class="group">
      <span class="group-title">Experimental</span>
      <label><input type="checkbox" id="toggle-exp">Use nearest weather station</label>
    </div>
    <div class="group">
      <button id="btn-locate">Use my location</button>
      <button id="btn-refresh">Refresh</button>
    </div>
  </div>
  <p id="layer-status" class="hint"></p>
  <p id="zoom-caption" class="hint" style="display:none">Zoomed in: each bubble marks a town. PSI is predicted per NEA region, so towns in the same region share one predicted value. Zoom out to bring the regional bubbles back.</p>
  <p id="regional-caption" class="hint" style="display:none">Regional haze view: each circle shows the forecast PM2.5 at that place (next 24 hours), converted to a PSI-equivalent. Arrows show where the wind is blowing toward. Dashed lines mark places where the wind points toward Singapore.</p>

  <div class="panel" id="forecast-panel" style="display:none">
    <div class="panel-title">Hour-by-hour PSI forecast <span id="fc-when" style="font-weight:400;color:#9A9A9A"></span></div>
    <input type="range" id="lead-slider" min="0" max="24" step="1" value="0" aria-label="Hours ahead">
    <div class="fc-quick">
      <button data-lead="0">Now</button><button data-lead="3">+3 h</button><button data-lead="6">+6 h</button>
      <button data-lead="12">+12 h</button><button data-lead="18">+18 h</button><button data-lead="24">+24 h</button>
    </div>
    <div id="fc-chart"></div>
    <div id="fc-summary" style="margin-top:8px"></div>
    <div class="guide-note">PSI is NEA's 24-hour index, so it changes slowly from hour to hour. These forecasts use only each region's PSI history (now, 6 hours ago and 24 hours ago), not weather. Chart lines are the five regions, with the one being described in white. On held-out test data these forecasts beat "no change" by about 8 to 11% from +3 h to +24 h; at +1 h the latest reading is used. <span id="fc-lagnote"></span></div>
  </div>

  <div class="legend">
    <div id="legend-bar" class="legend-bar"></div>
    <div class="legend-ticks"><span>0</span><span>100</span><span>200</span><span>300</span></div>
    <div class="legend-caption">Predicted PSI for the time shown (blue = clean air, maroon = extreme)</div>
  </div>

  <div class="panel" id="haze-panel">
    <div class="panel-title">Regional haze outlook for Singapore</div>
    <div id="haze-body">Loading regional air quality and wind forecasts...</div>
    <details class="how">
      <summary>How this outlook works</summary>
      <div class="how-body">
        <ol>
          <li>The page downloads forecast PM2.5 (fine particles) and wind for 11 places in Indonesia and Malaysia, plus the wind over Singapore.</li>
          <li>PM2.5 is averaged over the next 24 hours and converted to a PSI-equivalent using NEA's 24-hour PM2.5 bands (PSI 100 is about 55 &micro;g/m&sup3;).</li>
          <li>For each place it checks whether the wind at that place and over Singapore both point from there toward Singapore: within about 45&deg; counts as "toward", within about 70&deg; as "partly toward".</li>
          <li>The outlook is <b>High</b> if a place at PSI-equivalent 100 or more is strongly upwind and could arrive within 48 hours at current wind speeds. It is <b>Moderate</b> if the wind is only partly favourable, or a place at 75 or more is strongly upwind. Otherwise it is <b>Low</b>.</li>
        </ol>
        This is a simple rule-based indicator, not a trained model, and its thresholds have not yet been tested against past haze events. The data are model forecasts on a coarse grid of about 45 km, the places are sample points rather than fire locations, and real haze transport depends on winds at several heights. For official information, check NEA and the ASEAN Specialised Meteorological Centre.
      </div>
    </details>
  </div>

  <div class="panel" id="activity-guide">
    <div class="panel-title">What can you do outdoors at different PSI levels?</div>
    <div id="activity-body" class="act-grid"></div>
    <div class="guide-note">These are examples to help you plan, based on the idea in NEA's health advisory that prolonged or strenuous outdoor exertion is what to cut back as PSI rises. They are not medical advice. People with asthma or heart or lung conditions, older adults, pregnant women and young children should follow their doctor's advice and NEA's current advisory. The card for the worst-affected region (or the spot you picked) is outlined.</div>
  </div>

  <div class="panel" id="rec-guide">
    <div class="panel-title">How PSI is shown at outdoor recreation areas</div>
    <div id="rec-guide-rows"></div>
    <div class="guide-note">Each recreation area gets a marker coloured by its region's predicted PSI, with the number inside. Courts and playgrounds from OpenStreetMap use the same colours as small dots, football fields as squares and sports complexes as diamonds. The activity guide is a simplified version of NEA's PSI health advisory bands, so check nea.gov.sg for official advice.</div>
  </div>

  <div id="selected" class="panel">Click anywhere on the map, or tap a recreation area, court or playground, to see the predicted PSI for that spot.</div>
  <div id="exp-panel" class="panel" style="display:none"></div>
  <div id="inputs" class="panel" style="display:none"></div>

  <p class="footer">
    Hour-by-hour forecasts come from separate linear models, one per region and per hour ahead (2 to 24; +1 hour simply uses the latest reading, because the model did not beat it), trained on NEA's hourly PSI history from April 2014 to August 2026 with the latest 20% held out for testing. Average test error versus a "no change" baseline, in PSI points: +3 h 1.40 vs 1.53, +6 h 2.43 vs 2.71, +12 h 4.12 vs 4.64, +18 h 5.50 vs 6.20, +24 h 6.64 vs 7.38, a gain of about 8 to 11%. "Tomorrow's average" comes from the weather-based models described next.<br><br>
    Five linear regression models, one per NEA region, trained on Admiralty weather station data and each region's PSI, April 2014 to November 2017 (n = 979 days per region).
    Test MAE versus a naive baseline (tomorrow = today): North 5.71 vs 6.07, South 6.16 vs 6.68, East 5.84 vs 6.33, West 6.12 vs 6.62, Central 6.88 vs 7.44.<br><br>
    Limitations: PSI is reported per region, not per street, so any spot you pick gets its region's prediction. Region borders are approximated by whichever NEA region centre is nearest. The clean map is a simplified outline, not a survey-grade map. All regions use the same weather inputs. The live version uses the current instant weather reading in place of the daily summaries the models were trained on. The listed recreation areas are examples with approximate positions. Court, playground, football field and sports complex locations come from OpenStreetMap volunteers and may be incomplete, and the sports complex layer can include some indoor venues. When you zoom in, the town bubbles show the predicted value of the region each town belongs to, because the models predict one value per region.<br><br>
    Wind speeds from NEA's live feed are reported in knots and are converted to km/h to match the units the models were trained on. The experimental "nearest weather station" option gives each location the readings from its nearest NEA station instead of the island-wide average; it has not been validated.<br><br>
    The regional haze outlook is a separate rule-based indicator and does not change the model predictions above, which use local weather only. When the outlook is Moderate or High, those predictions may underestimate tomorrow's PSI.<br><br>
    Coastline data: &copy; OpenStreetMap contributors (ODbL), via geo-maps by Simone Primarosa. Country outlines: Natural Earth. Street map: &copy; OpenStreetMap contributors &copy; CARTO. Regional air quality and wind forecasts: <a href="https://open-meteo.com/" style="color:#7FB4FF">Open-Meteo.com</a> (CC BY 4.0), air quality containing modified Copernicus Atmosphere Monitoring Service (CAMS) information.
  </p>
</div>

